WEBVTT

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.070
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:25.280
You shouldn't have killed the Gyuki!

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:29.700
Kitaro?

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.130
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.190
Kitaro...

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.780
CHAPTER 22

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.700
BERSERK!! THE TERRIFYING <i>YOKAI</i>, GYUKI

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.330
We're here!

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.320
I wasn't expecting much,
but it's actually a pretty nice island.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.570
Not bad for a shopping street raffle.

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.880
Kitaro should hurry up and come.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.330
I fell asleep again.

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.330
But I'd rather sleep at home
than go on a trip.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.500
Catchick went to the trouble
of inviting us.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.920
It'd be an insult to waste it.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.090
I know.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:09.590
I invited him because the tour happened to
be for three people. And now he's late!

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.930
This island...

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.560
Kyosuke!

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:25.440
You and your lying grandfather
are seriously creepy.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.320
The legend of the Gyuki is true!

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.070
The Gyuki?

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:35.200
Tourists won't come if
a creepy legend like that gets spread.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.580
It hurts the island's image.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.960
My dad's hotel is finally making money.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.210
Leave the island already!

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:43.270
Hey!

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.580
What are you doing?!

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.340
We're not doing anything.
We're all friends.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.180
You're both tourists, aren't you?

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.600
Be sure to spend lots of money here.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.890
It'll help our allowances!

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.270
Are you okay?

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:07.210
Huh? An ancient terrifying legend
of this island?

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.740
Of course there's no such thing!

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:14.240
As you can see,
this is a trendy resort spot!

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.800
A trendy resort spot, huh?

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.830
Hey, coordinator!

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.870
Y-Yessir.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.500
I said we're an occult TV program,
didn't I?

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:28.710
We can't get any stories
from a bland tourist trap like this!

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.800
I wanted to take my money and run,
but these guys don't even pay up front.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:34.890
What was that?!

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:35.640
Nothing!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:40.020
Until a few years ago, this island was an
old fishing village and nothing like this.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.980
Who cares, director.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:46.150
This island has lots of girls
and seems fun. I like it!

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:47.460
See you later.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.030
Viewers tune in to see me, Jinguji.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:55.490
You can just make up some rural legend.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.120
But, Jinguji-san...

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.660
Hey, it's Koenji!

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.080
We watch you on TV!

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.040
Give us your autograph, Koenji!

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.040
It's not "Koenji!"
It's "Jinguji," you brats!

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.380
-He's not like on TV.
-He's mean.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:08.670
Forget the autograph.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.010
-Why you...!
-Now, now!

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.050
Do you kids live on this island?

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.050
Yeah.

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.680
Do you know any scary stories
passed down on this island?

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:21.930
N-No we don't.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.940
I'd be happy to pay you if you told me.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.060
Really?! How much?

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.020
Hey...

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:31.020
So there is one after all.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.030
My grandpa told me.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:36.410
Long ago, lots of people were
eaten by the Gyuki.

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:40.830
The island's peaceful now because
the Gyuki was sealed in the Gyuki Rock.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:41.910
The Gyuki Rock?

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:46.380
Yeah. That's why no one should
approach the Gyuki Rock.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.630
I see. So this island has
such a scary legend to it.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.570
But the people of this island
don't really believe it.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.090
Do you think it's a lie, too?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.810
No, I believe you.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.890
"The world you see
isn't all there is," right?

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.620
So that's Gyuki Rock, huh?

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:13.320
And this rock's supposed to be
some sort of lid to seal the monster, huh?

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.450
It looks like a pickling stone.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.110
Hey, Jinguji-san!

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.830
You can't get ratings
with a pickling stone, can you?

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:23.660
It's probably empty anyway.
Let's set something up.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.160
Heave ho!

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:28.520
Let's have a look.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.290
Well?

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.190
Jinguji-san?!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.220
Jinguji-sa--

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:43.100
Boo!

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:44.990
What are you doing?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:47.410
There's nothing there.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.100
Honestly.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:57.940
That's enough...

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.870
Jinguji-san?!

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.040
We should get help!

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.060
Hold on!

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.810
Something's coming up.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:15.040
This is...!

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.590
GYUKI

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:24.490
Hey, wait!

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:35.310
Cheers!

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.440
Yay!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.680
You idiot!

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.870
What's that? Whoa!

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:54.040
-Is it an event?
-That looks amazing! Is it real?

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:15.810
What?!

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.530
Mana, look after Kyosuke-kun!

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:21.860
Right!

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.240
What is that?!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.860
We're stopping it here!

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.490
Help!

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:19.820
You...

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:22.210
R-Run.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.560
Kitaro...

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.510
I'm coming!

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.970
Hair Needles!

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:36.690
Kitaro!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.150
Sorry for being late!

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.570
It's okay.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:41.500
I'll take care of this.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.510
Remote Controlled Geta!

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.880
Here I am!

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.570
Finger Guns!

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.080
Kitaro.

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.440
What was that?

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.200
I was almost digested there.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.330
Rat Man?!

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.710
J-Jinguji-san!

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.800
Man, Kitaro! What a relief!

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:44.590
What relief?! Is this your doing?

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:46.680
No way! I'm a victim this time!

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.140
Dad, what's that <i>yokai</i>?

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:50.550
It's the Gyuki.

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:55.350
It's just how Grandpa described it.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.810
The Gyuki really exists?

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.860
That's not all my grandpa told me.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.360
-Hey!
-What's wrong, Kyosuke-kun?

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:09.280
You shouldn't have killed the Gyuki!

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.860
What are you talking about?

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.870
Because...

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.370
Whoever kills the Gyuki...

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.870
Whoever kills the Gyuki...

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:28.590
Kitaro?

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.470
K-Kitaro...

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:53.950
Kitaro!

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:02.620
Whoever kills the Gyuki...

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:10.070
becomes the Gyuki!

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.140
<i>YOKAI</i> GYUKI

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.640
KITARO CHAYA (JINDAIJI TEMPLE, CHOFU CITY)

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:21.580
-<i>"I'll turn this into money."</i>
-<i>"This idiocy might be hiding a genius."</i>

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:22.580
<i>"No way."</i>

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.770
Kitaro! Kitaro!

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:35.660
Kitaro!

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:37.260
Stop, Catchick!

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.210
Cat-san, please! We have to run for now!

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:45.830
Grandpa might know
how to defeat the Gyuki!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.590
Let's go!

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:51.460
Defeat... Kitaro?

00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:03.600
Kyosuke, thank goodness you're safe!

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.270
But the Gyuki's destroying town!

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:08.280
Someone's broken the seal.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.610
That Gyuki is actually my son!

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:12.780
Wh-Who are you?

00:13:12.780 --> 00:13:14.740
Though he's being controlled,

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:19.080
I can't bear to see Kitaro harm
the people of this island any further!

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:22.160
Please lend us your knowledge
for what to do.

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.100
Hmm.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.170
At this rate the island will be completely
destroyed by the Gyuki.

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:33.110
But, no one can
escape the island with this storm.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:37.810
We're just tourists!
We don't intend to die on this island!

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:39.680
At least save our baby!

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.980
As president of my company,
if I die, my employees will be lost!

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:44.770
Just save me!

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:46.400
Huh? Mr. President?!

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.900
This is why no one should
approach the Gyuki Rock!

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.700
I'm so sorry!

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:02.660
We broke the rock's seal without thinking.
Please forgive us!

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.830
Him?

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.210
He's an outsider!

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:09.210
Why was an outsider at the Gyuki Rock?

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.670
This is all his fault!

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.840
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:14.170
There's one...

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:17.170
There's just one way.

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:24.350
According to legend, the one who sealed
the Gyuki in the Gyuki Rock

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:28.810
is the one worshiped at
this island's shrine, Karura-sama.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:34.030
Legend says, when things beyond the power
of the ancient people to solve occurred,

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:39.280
they gathered before Karura-sama's shrine
and focused their minds on praying.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:44.620
What's important is to unite our hearts
and bow our heads.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:48.710
If anyone holds any malice towards another
or hopes they alone will be saved

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:52.000
Karura-sama won't help us.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.630
That's impossible.
So, prayer's the only option?

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:58.510
Let's do it, everyone.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:02.140
Kyosuke-kun, show us to the shrine.

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.200
Okay.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.250
-Let's go, too!
-Yeah!

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.730
Oh, come on. Seriously?

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.530
Karura-sama is here?

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.430
Th-The Gyuki!

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.430
The Gyuki's coming this way!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.430
It's all over!

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:50.810
I'll lure it away.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:52.360
Everyone, summon Karura-sama.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:53.480
Cat-san.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.690
By yourself?!

00:15:54.690 --> 00:15:56.250
It's too dangerous!

00:15:57.420 --> 00:16:00.530
Catchick can do it. Let's trust her.

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:03.780
I won't last long. I'm counting on you!

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.390
Got it.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:10.040
Kitaro.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.300
Karura-sama.

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.110
-Karura-sama.
-Please help us!

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:31.020
Come on! You're fighting me!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:37.920
Please save us.

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:23.030
Hold it!

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:26.530
I'm your opponent here!

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.050
Kitaro!

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.550
-Karura-sama!
-Please!

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.220
-Please help us.
-Something, anything show up!

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:50.390
Karura-sama! Please!

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:17.230
Mana...

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:19.040
Daddy Eyeball-san...

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.400
Kyosuke-kun...

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:25.920
Everyone...

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:30.640
Kitaro...

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:46.570
Oh! Karura-sama!

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:54.810
Karura-sama, please save the people
of this island! Please save my son!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.480
I shall try.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.770
Karura... sama?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.910
Cat-san, are you okay?!

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:38.710
You did well, Catchick!

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:42.750
If Karura-sama defeats the Gyuki,
what happens to Kitaro?

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:44.300
I don't know...

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:48.800
But, Kitaro wouldn't want to hurt
the people of this island any further.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.930
You're right...

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.780
I'm sure he wouldn't.

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:54.740
I'm sorry, Kitaro...

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.430
I'm sorry.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.120
I've caught it.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.120
Kitaro...

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.140
Kitaro!

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.130
What, Catchick?

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:38.060
What in the world happened?

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:39.790
Kitaro...

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:43.920
What's wrong, Catchick?

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.130
Thank goodness!

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:52.660
I am one of the 28 guardians
of the thousand-armed Kannon.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.870
I am a god from a distant land,

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:58.080
but long ago
I came here to defeat the Gyuki.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:02.540
The Gyuki's true form is
a gas that alters living cells.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:06.090
When possessed by it,
one takes the form of the Gyuki.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:09.210
It latches onto a host until it dies,
after which

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:13.650
it moves to the nearest living being,
allowing it to live for centuries.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:17.970
So the Gyuki is now a gas
inside that <i>furoshiki</i>?

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:21.270
That's right. But it's not dead.

